Vulnerability data

This product uses data from the NVD API but is not endorsed or certified by the
NVD. The built-in application data (internal/appvuln/data) is derived from the
National Vulnerability Database (https://nvd.nist.gov), a public work of the
U.S. government.

The vulnerability data that `feed sync` downloads at run time stays under each
publisher's own terms; it is not part of this distribution. See the Data sources
section of README.md.

Test fixtures contain short excerpts of published vendor data, used to test the
parsers:
- Canonical Ubuntu OVAL / USN excerpts (testdata/feeds and cmd/openness-resolver/testdata):
  Canonical Ltd., https://security-metadata.canonical.com/oval/ ; Ubuntu security notices
  are published under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://github.com/canonical/ubuntu-security-notices).
- Microsoft Security Update Guide CVRF documents (internal/resolver/testdata/msrc):
  Microsoft Corporation, https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide , Microsoft Terms of Use.
- OSV records (testdata/raw/osv, testdata/feeds/osv/pypi): https://osv.dev ; GitHub Security Advisories and
  the PyPA advisory database, CC BY 4.0.
